NAME
    stress - Repeatedly exercise managed-runtime and ring-3 userland subsystems.

SYNOPSIS
    stress [all|exceptions|eh|ehstress|gc|dispatch|generics|collections|typeloader|abi|userland] [iterations]

DOMAIN
    userland

DESCRIPTION
    Runs the stress controller as a real ring-3 Inu process. Inu exposes exactly three
    native syscall operations: Get, Set and Event. Stress progress is emitted with
    Event(ConsoleOutput); the shell does not poll shared progress state. Managed runtime
    stages are requested with Set(StressControl), while completion is read with
    Get(StressStatus). Event payloads are copied into a bounded kernel queue and rendered
    by the GUI role worker. Managed stages run on the persistent Background role worker
    with a normal kernel/GC stack; no scheduler creation or context switch occurs on a
    syscall stack.

    The path therefore also validates package parsing, ELF64 loading, a private process
    address space, IRETQ ring-3 entry, SYSCALL/SYSRETQ, Get/Set/Event dispatch and
    controlled process exit back to ring 0.

    all          managed runtime suites plus the end-to-end userland process suite
    exceptions   throw/catch/finally, cross-frame unwind and rethrow (aliases: eh, ehstress)
    gc           mature collection, roots, reclamation, reuse and finalization
    dispatch     class virtual, interface dispatch, casts and variance
    generics     dictionaries, GVMs, constrained calls, constructors and statics
    collections  List, Dictionary, Queue and Stack mutation/enumeration/EH
    typeloader   NativeLayout type lookup plus generic static/default-ctor paths
    abi          object, boxing, handles, delegates, primitive and MethodTable ABI
    userland     application package -> process -> ring 3 -> Get/Set/Event -> exit -> cleanup

LIMITS
    all/gc/userland: 16 iterations
    generics/collections/abi: 250 iterations
    typeloader: 500 iterations
    exceptions/dispatch: 1000 iterations

EXAMPLES
    stress all 2
    stress userland 4
    stress gc 3
    stress ehstress 32
    stress generics 100
    stress typeloader 100

BOOT POLICY
    Exception/unwind stress is not run automatically during normal OS boot. The former
    EHStress boot workload is owned by this command; use `stress exceptions`, `stress eh`
    or `stress ehstress` when you want to run it explicitly.

ELAPSED TIME
    Long-running stress/selftest packages request one live elapsed-time status line from
    the presentation layer. The line is updated in place once per second and is not a
    stress-progress polling channel; stage progress still arrives only through Event(ConsoleOutput).

SEE ALSO
    selftest

Live progress
-------------
Stress/selftest output is emitted by the ring-3 controller with Event(ConsoleOutput).
Exceptions, dispatch, generics, collections, typeloader, ABI, GC and userland are
announced in order and each result is printed before the next stage is submitted. No
shell-side stress progress polling or single-slot coalescing is used. Immediately before
controlled process exit the controller prints an exit marker; if the VM stops, the last
visible Event-delivered line identifies whether failure occurred inside a stage or on the
ring-3-to-ring-0 exit path.
